{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"My dearest Marie,\n\nThe air in Vienna is thick with culture, and I am somewhat exhausted by the excess of it. I spent three hours today in the Esterhazy gallery. The Prince, hearing a professor from Berlin had arrived, insisted I see the private cabinet. It is a magnificent collection, though I found myself thinking of how such private hoarding contrasts with the public spirit of a state.\n\nI dined with Professor Sonnleitner and a man from Padua. We spoke of antiquities, but mostly of the wine, which was excellent. In the evening, I attended Rossini’s *Corradino*. The music is dazzling, full of that Italian lightness, though I confess I found the drama somewhat thin. It moves the senses, certainly, but does it move the spirit?\n\nI am tired but content. Think of me by the fire in Berlin.\n\nYours ever,\nG.W.F. Hegel"}}],"created":1795080345,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":193,"prompt_tokens":951,"total_tokens":1144,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-K8acJnYKosVOHZ46uaYPbAjQ9Z5MIpYG","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":951,"prompt_ms":926.995,"prompt_per_token_ms":0.974758149316509,"prompt_per_second":1025.8955010544826,"predicted_n":193,"predicted_ms":4767.229,"predicted_per_token_ms":24.829317708333335,"predicted_per_second":40.274968959955565}}